('qn_jameco', 'Jameco, village by the Beaver Pond', 'lenape_settlement', 1656,
 ('X', 'Beaver Road', '158th Street', (-73.7985, 40.7003)), 8, 80, 'medium',
 WIG + 'DOCUMENTED: Bolton station 101, "A native settlement seems to have existed near the Beaver pond ... \'The beaver path\' led from the native village to the pond"; Parker (Queens no. 8) after Thompson: "Village of the Jameco Indians on a creek a mile south of the present village of Jamaica". The pond lay south of today\'s Beaver Road. End: Rustdorp (Jamaica) settled 1656. ESTIMATE: count, spread; Bolton: "The exact location of the [lodges] has not been recorded".', BP),
('qn_hook_creek', 'Village site and shell heap near Hook Creek', 'lenape_settlement', 1685,
 ('P', -73.7372, 40.6502), 6, 70, 'low',
 WIG + 'DOCUMENTED: Parker (Queens no. 11) "Village site and shell heap near Hook Creek station on the road to Far Rockaway". ' + UND + 'ESTIMATE: count, spread; spot on the Queens side of the creek good to about 700 m; end = the Rockaway sale of 1685 by Pamas / Tackapousha (Bolton 1920; Wikipedia, Far Rockaway).', PA),
